id: disarm
name: Disarm
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
usageLimit: 1/round
exploitOnLoss: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Clash of your Strike against their Strike or Dodge, at an Opponent wielding a Weapon within your Melee Range: win, and the
  Weapon is out of their grip.
text: >
  Disarm Maneuver [1/Round]: Take a Weapon away from your foe!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: If you fail the clash for the Disarm Maneuver, trigger the Exploit Maneuver of the target.
  –Effect: Target an Opponent wielding a Weapon within your Melee Range. Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge). If you win, the Weapon is removed from their grip and lands on a Square adjacent to that Opponent of your choice.

---

# The one targeted: an Opponent - of another disposition - wielding a Weapon, within your Melee Range (use-maneuver.mjs). The
# Clash, Strike against their Strike or Dodge (chat.mjs postDisarmClash). Won: which Weapon, where they wield several, asked of
# you - no longer wielded; where it lands, the map's. Lost: their Exploit offered on its card (`exploitOnLoss`).
